[strategy/guidance/application/nodejs/GUID-TEC-NODE-002-bff-implementation.md#42-per-request-timeout-budgets]

### 4.2 Per-Request Timeout Budgets

Per STD-TEC-NODE-001 §8.2, all outbound calls must have explicit timeouts. For BFF aggregation calls, set a per-call timeout and a total request budget:

```typescript
// src/utils/fetch-with-timeout.ts
export async function fetchWithTimeout(
  url: string,
  options: RequestInit = {},
  timeoutMs: number = 5000
): Promise<Response> {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeoutMs);
  try {
    const response = await fetch(url, { ...options, signal: controller.signal });
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new UpstreamError(url, `HTTP ${response.status}`);
    }
    return response;
  } finally {
    clearTimeout(timeoutId);
  }
}
```

Set individual call timeouts conservatively. For a total request budget of 10 seconds across three parallel calls, set each call timeout at 8 seconds — the parallel execution means the total time is bounded by the slowest call plus overhead.

