### 4.3 Response Shaping

The BFF is responsible for mapping upstream service responses to client-specific data shapes. Define explicit TypeScript types for both the upstream response and the client response, and write an explicit mapper function:

```typescript
// src/mappers/member.mapper.ts
import { MemberApiResponse } from '../types/upstream/member-api.types';
import { MemberSummary } from '../types/client/dashboard.types';

export function toMemberSummary(upstream: MemberApiResponse): MemberSummary {
  return {
    id: upstream.memberId,
    displayName: `${upstream.firstName} ${upstream.lastName}`,
    planName: upstream.planDetails.displayName,
    coverageStatus: upstream.eligibility.status,
    primaryCareProvider: upstream.pcpDetails?.displayName ?? null,
  };
}
```

Explicit mapper functions are testable independently of the HTTP layer and make the client/upstream contract visible.

