### 5.1 Access Token Validation

The BFF validates bearer tokens from browser clients using the same JWT + JWKS pattern as other backend services. See [GUID-TEC-NODE-001 §4.1](../../security/nodejs/GUID-TEC-NODE-001-secure-microservice-implementation.md#41-jwt-authentication-ptn-sec-api-002) for the complete `authMiddleware` implementation.

For browser-facing BFFs using OIDC session cookies rather than bearer tokens, use `express-openid-connect` and validate the session on each request:

```typescript
import { requiresAuth, getAccessToken } from 'express-openid-connect';

// Protected routes require a valid OIDC session
router.get('/dashboard', requiresAuth(), dashboardController.getDashboard);
```

