[strategy/guidance/application/nodejs/GUID-TEC-NODE-002-bff-implementation.md#7-error-normalisation]

## 7. Error Normalisation

The BFF is the last error handler before the browser client. It must:

1. Classify upstream errors and map them to appropriate HTTP status codes for the client.
2. Return a consistent error envelope per [PTN-APP-API-011](../../../../patterns/application/api-microservices/PTN-APP-API-011-error-response-pattern.md).
3. Never expose internal service names, upstream error messages, stack traces, or any detail that would help an attacker understand the backend topology.

```typescript
// src/middleware/error-handler.middleware.ts
import { Request, Response, NextFunction } from 'express';
import { logger } from '../utils/logger';
import { AppError, UpstreamError } from '../utils/errors';

interface ClientErrorResponse {
  error: {
    code: string;
    message: string;
    correlationId: string;
    timestamp: string;
  };
}

function buildErrorResponse(
  code: string,
  message: string,
  correlationId: string
): ClientErrorResponse {
  return {
    error: {
      code,
      message,
      correlationId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    },
  };
}

export function errorHandlerMiddleware(
  error: unknown,
  req: Request,
  res: Response,
  _next: NextFunction
): void {
  const correlationId = req.correlationId;

  if (error instanceof UpstreamError) {
    // Map upstream 4xx to BFF 502 — the client should not receive the upstream's
    // internal error details, only that a dependency failed.
    logger.error({ err: error, correlationId }, 'Upstream service error');
    res.status(502).json(
      buildErrorResponse('UPSTREAM_ERROR', 'A required service is temporarily unavailable.', correlationId)
    );
    return;
  }

  if (error instanceof AppError) {
    if (error.statusCode >= 500) {
      logger.error({ err: error, correlationId }, 'BFF server error');
    } else {
      logger.warn({ err: error, correlationId }, 'BFF application error');
    }
    res.status(error.statusCode).json(buildErrorResponse(error.code, error.message, correlationId));
    return;
  }

  // Programmer errors or unexpected conditions
  logger.error({ err: error, correlationId }, 'Unhandled BFF error');
  res.status(500).json(
    buildErrorResponse('INTERNAL_ERROR', 'An unexpected error occurred.', correlationId)
  );
}
```

**Upstream error classification:**

| Upstream Response | BFF Response to Client |
|---|---|
| 400 from upstream (bad request sent by BFF) | 500 — indicates a BFF bug, not a client error |
| 401 from upstream | 401 — token relay failure; client must re-authenticate |
| 403 from upstream | 403 — scope or permission issue |
| 404 from upstream | 404 — resource not found |
| 429 from upstream | 503 — BFF is being rate-limited by a downstream service |
| 500/503 from upstream | 502/503 — upstream service error |
| Timeout | 504 — upstream service timed out |

