[strategy/guidance/application/nodejs/GUID-TEC-NODE-002-bff-implementation.md#82-health-check-propagation]

### 8.2 Health Check Propagation

The BFF `/health` endpoint must report the health of its downstream dependencies and reflect degraded status when critical dependencies are unavailable:

```typescript
// src/routes/health.router.ts
import { Router } from 'express';
import { asyncRoute } from '../utils/async-route';
import { memberCircuitBreaker } from '../services/member.service';

const router = Router();

router.get(
  '/',
  asyncRoute(async (_req, res) => {
    const memberServiceHealthy = !memberCircuitBreaker.state.open;

    const status = memberServiceHealthy ? 'ok' : 'degraded';
    const httpStatus = memberServiceHealthy ? 200 : 503;

    res.status(httpStatus).json({
      status,
      dependencies: {
        memberService: memberServiceHealthy ? 'ok' : 'circuit-open',
      },
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    });
  })
);

export { router as healthRouter };
```

When the health endpoint returns `503`, Kubernetes liveness/readiness probes will stop routing traffic to the degraded BFF instance.

