### 9.1 Cache-Control Headers

The BFF must set explicit `Cache-Control` headers on responses. Default to `no-store` for all endpoints that return user-specific or PHI-adjacent data:

```typescript
// Default for authenticated, user-specific responses
res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'no-store');

// For reference data (plan codes, provider directories) that is safe to cache
res.setHeader('Cache-Control', 'private, max-age=300');
```

Do not set `Cache-Control: public` for any endpoint that returns data from an authenticated session. CDN or shared proxy caches would serve one user's data to another.

